C. Key divergence details
  1. Category normalization: src/ has toCategoryCode() to map "Equity - Large Cap"
     → EQ-LC; CIFRAA assumes data is already in short-code format.
  2. Goal eligibility (wealth_creation): src/ allows EQ-, HY-, DT- categories;
     CIFRAA restricts to EQ- only.
  3. Expense scoring: src/ uses 1 - (ratio - 0.8) / 1.2; CIFRAA uses
     1 - min(ratio, 2) × 0.35.
  4. Completeness penalty: src/ penalizes missing CAGR/vol/Sharpe at 15% each;
     CIFRAA penalizes all fields uniformly at 5% each.
  5. Age penalty: src/ penalizes funds <5 years; CIFRAA does not.
  6. Conservative promotion: CIFRAA promotes conservative→moderate for
     long-horizon wealth creation; src/ never promotes.
  7. Aggressive demotion: CIFRAA demotes on short OR beginner; src/ requires both.
  8. Diversification: src/ delegates to portfolioConstructor.ts (core-satellite,
     AMC cap=1); CIFRAA has inline diversify() with ETF caps, arbitrage caps.

